From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] luci-mod-system: remove stale mount crontab grant
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

Backport OpenWrt LuCI commit 903af348552f ("luci-mod-system: cleanup
mount ACL group"). The mount-management ACL does not need write access
to root's crontab. Keeping that stale grant allows a delegated mount
operator to escalate to root, as tracked by GHSA-v5f9-62c7-cw29.

---
 .../root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-system.json           | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/luci-mod-system/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-system.json b/modules/luci-mod-system/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-system.json
--- a/modules/luci-mod-system/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-system.json
+++ b/modules/luci-mod-system/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-system.json
@@ -130,7 +130,6 @@
 		},
 		"write": {
 			"file": {
-				"/etc/crontabs/root": [ "write" ],
 				"/bin/umount": [ "exec" ],
 				"/sbin/block": [ "exec" ]
 			},
-- 
2.51.0
